# Conversations as chains (Docs/Design/62-talk.md, section 2; phase 4): a rule hands the next beat to the other
# speaker, who answers with their own best rule for it, so every reply is chosen by the replier's own facts. A start;
# phase 7 writes the families properly.

# Prices: the poor complain, and each answers as they are.
rule prices_complain_poor
when concept=talk.prices self.wealth=poor|destitute topic.dir=up
say #oath#. I'll not eat this week at #topic.price#. | #topic.price#? For #topic.what#? #robbery#.
then other: prices.answer_complaint
remember self: complained_prices 1d

rule prices_complain_again
when concept=talk.prices self.mem.complained_prices topic.dir=up
priority 1
say Still #topic.price#. I said it yesterday and I'll say it again. | Dearer every day#tag#.
then other: prices.answer_complaint

rule prices_answer_merchant
when concept=prices.answer_complaint self.role=merchant
say Roads are bad, #address#. I pay more, you pay more. | Blame the carters, not me.
remember pair: talked_money 7d

rule prices_answer_poor
when concept=prices.answer_complaint self.wealth=poor|destitute
say #agree#. We'll all go hungry together. | Don't I know it.

rule prices_answer_rich
when concept=prices.answer_complaint self.wealth=rich
say Is it? I hadn't noticed. | Surely not so very much.

rule prices_answer
when concept=prices.answer_complaint
say #agree#. It's the caravans, they say. | #agree#. Nothing to be done.

# Two friends passing: a greeting, and the answer as the answerer is today.
rule greet_friend
when concept=react.friend
cooldown 6h
say #greet#, #pet#! | #greet#, #pet#. Keeping well?
then other: greet.answer

rule greet_answer
when concept=greet.answer
say #greet#! Can't stop. | #greet#, #pet#. Well enough.

rule greet_answer_tired
when concept=greet.answer tired=yes
say #tired.capitalize#. Don't ask. | Ask me after I've slept.

rule greet_answer_mourning
when concept=greet.answer mourning=kin
priority 3
say ... Thank you for asking. | Not good. Not today.

rule greet_answer_working
when concept=greet.answer working=yes shift=during
say Can't stop, I'm at work. | Later, #pet#. Work.
